  "body": "<!-- ⚠️ If you do not respect this template, your issue will be closed -->\r\n<!-- ⚠️ Make sure to browse the opened and closed issues to confirm this idea does not exist. -->\r\n\r\n### What is the expected enhancement?\r\n\r\nIn [this comment](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-nature/issues/307#issuecomment-894053897) I proposed to add some checks on the generated excitations as used in the `UCC` Ansatz, [here](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-nature/blob/main/qiskit_nature/circuit/library/ansatzes/ucc.py#L293).\r\nThis idea was motivated after seeing [this](https://quantumcomputing.stackexchange.com/questions/20749/define-customized-excitation-for-the-unitary-coupled-cluster-ucc-algorithm-in) stackexchange question. Since #322 only fixes the documentation aspects of #307 I am extracting this improvement to a separate issue.\r\n\r\nPossible checks which could be done are:\r\n- excitations are a list of pairs\r\n- each pair consists of two tuples of identical length\r\n- all indices within a pair are unique\r\n\r\nA potential location for these checks is the `UCC.excitations` property setter method.\r\nThe `__init__` method should then make use of that setter to trigger those checks, too.",
